Z||000000||fierodave||03-17-2000||11:33 PM||||<BR>hello all this is some info you need to know  have a great night  <BR>FD<BR>          FIERO RECALLS <BR>      TILL DEATH DO US PART<BR>If you called the dealer and they told you the recall work was done on your car  there fibbing!!!!!!(did they say the recalls were done, or that there were no open recalls?)  big difference!!!!!  <BR>They(the dealers) have no way to check by your vin number anymore!  <BR>In jan of 99 pontiac purged there computers of all fiero related material dealing in Vins. more proof  ask them for a copy of the recall work done   lol  they don't have any! <BR>so i suggest you go down there and see if they can bring it up on a screen  lol   they will say  hmmmmm  i wonder why i can't   lol<BR>all recalls on the fiero's are in affect regardless of who the owner is and the miles on the car  from the date the recall was announnced until forever!!!!!!!!!!!!  <BR>I have had three Fiero's recall work done in the last year and it took a trip there every time!  YOU HAVE TO GET THE DEALER TO AGREE TO LOOK AT THE CAR!!!<BR>within 30 seconds with there Recall manual(yep they have one) in there hand they can tell! And forget PM cares  that's a bunch of Crap  and pontiac connot make a dealer look at it either,  they can strongly suggest the dealer do it as a jesture that's it!   if you get no cooperation from your dealer tell them you would like the name and number of there district zone rep or ask if they would contact them for you  9 out 10 times  that's enough to get them to look at the car Once they agree to look at it,  your over the hump  and they will do the work  and it's free!!!!!!!!  I talk from knowing and doing  thanks for the space<BR>FD ||||reg||14
